<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 28 April, from 224 to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ardashir-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/224">224 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,802 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ardashir I defeats Artabanus IV at the Battle of Hormozdgan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hormozdgan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a> defeated the Parthian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artabanus-iv">Artabanus IV</a>, who was killed. The victory ended almost five centuries of Parthian rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and marked the start of the Sasanian era.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hormozdgan">Battle of Hormozdgan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/357">357 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,669 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II makes his only visit to Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in triumph for the first time. The historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> described his astonishment at the Forum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> and other monuments.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1192">1192 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">834 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Conrad of Montferrat is assassinated in Tyre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a>, who had held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, was murdered in the city by two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassins</a>. He had been elected king of Jerusalem only days before.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Order of Assassins</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1253">1253 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">773 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nichiren first proclaims Namu Myōhō Renge Kyō in public</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to one of his letters, the Japanese monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nichiren">Nichiren</a> lectured at Seicho-ji Temple on the supremacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lotus-sutra">Lotus Sutra</a>, then first declared Namu Myōhō Renge Kyō in public atop Mount Kiyosumi. The phrase became central to Nichiren <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nichiren">Nichiren</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fletcher Christian leads the mutiny on the Bounty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mutineers seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-bounty">HMS Bounty</a> and set Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bligh">William Bligh</a> adrift with 18 men in an open launch. Bligh navigated some 6,700 km to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> with the loss of only one man.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1818">1818 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">208 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rush-Bagot Agreement is proclaimed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Monroe proclaimed the Anglo-American agreement limiting warships on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-champlain">Lake Champlain</a>. It helped demilitarise the border between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Partisans shoot Mussolini near Lake Como</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> and Clara Petacci were shot by partisans at Giulino di Mezzegra. The next day their bodies were hung upside down in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>'s Piazzale Loreto.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1952">1952 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">74 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan regains its sovereignty as the Allied occupation ends</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-francisco">Treaty of San Francisco</a> came into force, ending the Allied occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> that had begun in 1945. A US-Japan security treaty took effect the same day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles de Gaulle resigns as President of France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After voters rejected his referendum on regional and Senate reform, de Gaulle stepped down at noon. He had led the Fifth Republic since its foundation in 1958.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 28 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-iv-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-iv-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward IV of England</span><span class="tp">1442–1483</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yi-sun-sin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Yi Sun-sin</span><span class="tp">1545–1598</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-kaunda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kenneth-kaunda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kenneth Kaunda</span><span class="tp">1924–2021</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/saddam-hussein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saddam Hussein</span><span class="tp">1937–2006</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
